{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environmentvalues\/colorscheme"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues\/colorScheme","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"colorScheme","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ColorScheme","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ColorScheme","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI11ColorSchemeO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Read this environment value from within a view to find out if OpenSwiftUI","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is currently displaying the view using the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ColorScheme\/light","type":"reference"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ColorScheme\/dark","type":"reference"},{"text":" appearance. The value that you receive depends on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whether the user has enabled Dark Mode, possibly superseded by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the configuration of the current presentation’s view hierarchy.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Environment(\\.colorScheme) private var colorScheme","","var body: some View {","    Text(colorScheme == .dark ? \"Dark\" : \"Light\")","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can set the "},{"code":"colorScheme","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" environment value directly,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but that usually isn’t what you want. Doing so changes the color"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scheme of the given view and its child views but "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the views"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"above it in the view hierarchy. Instead, set a color scheme using the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View\/preferredColorScheme(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier, which also propagates the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value up through the view hierarchy to the enclosing presentation, like"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a sheet or a window."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When adjusting your app’s user interface to match the color scheme,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consider also checking the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues\/colorSchemeContrast","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property, which reflects a system-wide contrast setting that the user","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"controls. For information about using color and contrast in your app,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/accessibility\/overview\/color-and-contrast\/","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you only need to provide different colors or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"images for different color s